WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:08.800
Samwell Tarly is more than just your average
loyal sidekick. Sure, he's loyal, honest,

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.759
and his heart of gold is too nice for this
world. But there's more to him than that.

00:00:13.759 --> 00:00:18.830
In fact, Sam might just be the most important
Game of Thrones character of all. Season six's

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:23.289
finale episode dropped a giant Easter Egg
seemingly putting him at the center of...everything.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:30.300
Oh, and just in case you weren't aware...spoilers
ahead.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.930
What Sam Saw in the Citadel

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:37.040
When Sam, Gilly, and the baby finally arrived
in Oldtown, he got his first look at that

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:42.660
jaw-dropping library. And we spotted a special
something lingering above him: a spherical

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:47.370
chandelier system...that's awfully similar
to the astrolabe that shines in the show's

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:52.050
intro credits. That's right, the glowing golden
orb that comes into focus and kicks off every

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.350
episode had always seemed like something of
a lovely—but unimportant—visual before.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:01:01.830
But now that it's been seen hanging in the
Citadel's massive library, its purpose might

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.900
be getting clearer...

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.259
Sam's Song of Ice and Fire?

00:01:06.259 --> 00:01:10.750
As pointed out by an article from TV Guide,
George R. R. Martin, author of The Song of

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.310
Ice and Fire novels the show is based on,
has long admitted to being inspired by that

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:21.010
other double-RR-middle-named fantasy legend:
J.R.R. Tolkien, and his iconic Lord of the

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:25.270
Rings series. Samwell Tarly is thought to
be a tribute to Tolkien's character with a

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:31.030
similar name: Samwise Gamgee. That Sam ended
up being pretty important, as he was ultimately

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:35.190
given the task of finishing the story of "the
one ring to rule them all" and how it was

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.020
destroyed by Frodo.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.409
"The last pages are for you Sam."

00:01:39.409 --> 00:01:43.470
Martin has famously promised that his own
story ending would reflect Tolkien's "bittersweet"

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:48.250
ending style. So will Samwell Tarly do for
The Song of Ice and Fire what Samwise Gamgee

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:52.310
did for those little guys and the jewelry?
Does he write the story of Jon Snow versus

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:55.840
the White Walkers at the Citadel, under the
light of the big golden orb?

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.100
Is he the reason that book six missed its
damn deadline?

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.190
Research to the Rescue

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.520
Forget the fact that Daenerys Targaryen is
on her way to oust Mad Queen Cersei from the

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.519
Iron Throne. And that Jon Snow has been declared
King in the North and may have earned the

00:02:10.519 --> 00:02:15.810
jealous ire of his sister-slash-cousin Sansa
Stark—and Littlefinger. Those are but battles

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:20.939
in the grand scheme of things. The true war,
of course, will come once the Night King figures

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:25.310
out a way to get his army of White Walkers
past the Wall. And Sam's access to Oldtown's

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:30.099
bevy of books may help him find a more efficient
way for people to kill the undead.

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:32.579
Building a Better Dragonglass

00:02:32.579 --> 00:02:36.409
Sam's killed a White Walker himself with a
dragonglass dagger, so he already knows the

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:41.159
strength and resilience of the enemy's forces
and obsidian's effect on them. He also knows

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:44.989
about the stockpile of dragonglass in the
island of Dragonstone, thanks to the late

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:49.749
Stannis Baratheon. But the North's forces
are outnumbered, and the Walkers are tireless,

00:02:49.749 --> 00:02:54.909
fast, and bloodthirsty. So, really, it might
be on Sam to discover a better way to defeat

00:02:54.909 --> 00:02:59.159
those seemingly unkillable forces of darkness.
Could his good-hearted nature help convince

00:02:59.159 --> 00:03:01.459
Daenerys to lend her dragons to the cause?

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:04.079
Because that might be super helpful.

00:03:04.079 --> 00:03:07.139
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:03:07.139 --> 00:03:11.249
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know if you think Sam is as important

00:03:11.249 --> 00:03:11.749
as we do...

